  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 AM EDT Sat Jun 27 2026\n\n- Extreme heat risk next week\n\nMain weather concern continues to be the onset of heat and \nhumidity after the weekend. After a comfortable weekend...hot\ntemperatures and humidity build Monday and remain through at \nleast the end of the week. High temperatures in the mid 90s at \nleast can be expected with lows likely staying in at least the mid\n70s. Heat index values over 100 likely Tuesday through Thursday \nat least with potential for 110 plus remaining...especially as you\nmove east and south across lower Michigan. \n\nThe lack of cooling at night and the expected humidity in place\nday and night through the week will bring extreme heat hazards to\nlower Michigan. Preparations should be made to mitigate the\nimpacts of extreme heat to people and animals before the heat\narrives. \n\nHeat safety tips and resources can be found by visiting:\nweather.gov/heat\n\nSome relief from the extreme heat may occur at the end of the\nweek...but prolonged summer temperatures in the 80s and maybe 90s\nare expected to persist through at least the holiday weekend...if\nnot through the entire first week of July.  \n\n- Chances for showers and storms next week \n\nWith this much heat and humidity in place it is not uncommon for\nus to see some afternoon/evening isolated storms or more organized\nactivity as shortwaves move through the Great Lakes region. Best\nchance for showers/storms at this point still looks to be late\nSunday night and Monday and again maybe the middle to the end of \nthe week.",
